course: dictionary
lesson: 4609
title: Hiccough, hiccup, or a small problem?
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Hiccough» is an old spelling of «hiccup», the sudden, sharp «hic» sound you make when a muscle under your lungs jerks. In the story, «giving the Whale hiccoughs» means the Whale was making those sounds, so the meaning is the hiccup sound, not a problem.
explain: Look at the other words around it. In «a hiccough in our plans», there are no sounds and no whale, so the word must mean a small problem or delay. Try your meaning in the sentence: «a small problem in our plans» still makes sense, so you have probably got it right.
explain: Notice that the spelling tells you about the book. Older books may write «hiccough», but most people today write «hiccup». If you see «hiccough» in an old story, you do not need to worry: it is the same word, just spelled in an older way.
fact: «Hiccough» is an old spelling of «hiccup».
fact: A hiccup is a sudden, sharp «hic» sound made when a muscle under your lungs, called the diaphragm, tightens and jerks.
fact: As a noun, «hiccoughs» or «hiccups» can mean a short spell of these sounds, one after another.
fact: «A hiccough in our plans» means a small problem or delay.
fact: Hiccups usually stop by themselves. Some people say a fright cures them, but this has never been proven.
exercise: In the story, the Whale got «hiccoughs». What does this mean? | A kind of sailors' dance | *An old spelling of hiccups: a sudden «hic» sound | A long, low whale song | A loud splash in the sea
exercise: Which spelling do most people use today? | *Hiccup | Hiccough | Hickup | Hiccuup
exercise: «There was a hiccough in our plans.» What does hiccough mean here? | *A small problem or delay | A big party | A sudden hic sound | A long walk to school
test: What happens in your body when you have hiccups? | *A muscle under your lungs jerks and you breathe in suddenly | Your heart stops for a moment | Your ears fill with air | You sneeze three times
test: Why do hiccups usually stop? | They stop when you yell loudly | They stop only when you eat a sweet | They never stop unless you see a doctor | *They stop by themselves
exam: Which sentence uses hiccough to mean a small problem? | «The sea was calm and blue all day.» | *«There was a hiccough in our plans, so we met an hour later.» | «The Mariner danced a lively hornpipe.» | «The Whale let out a loud hiccough in the sea.»
